A Significant Data Fiduciary must, beyond the ordinary obligations of a Data Fiduciary,  

* appoint a Data Protection Officer who is based in India, reports to the board and is the grievance‑redressal contact [Section 10(2)(a)];  
* appoint an independent data auditor to conduct data audits [Section 10(2)(b)];  
* carry out periodic measures such as Data Protection Impact Assessments and audits, and any other prescribed measures [Section 10(2)(c)].

full.answer:
A Significant Data Fiduciary must, beyond the ordinary duties of a Data Fiduciary, :

- Appoint a Data Protection Officer who is based in India, reports to the board and is the grievance‑redressal contact [Section 10(2)(a)];
- Appoint an independent data auditor to conduct data audits [Section 10(2)(b)];
- Carry out additional measures such as periodic Data Protection Impact Assessments, periodic audits and any other prescribed measures [Section 10(2)(c)].

