A person is disqualified from being appointed or continuing as a Member of the Board if they:

- Have been adjudged an insolvent;  
- Have been convicted of an offence that the Central Government considers to involve moral turpitude;  
- Are physically or mentally incapable of acting as a Member;  
- Have a financial or other interest likely to prejudice their functions; or  
- Have abused their position such that their continuance would be prejudicial to public interest.  

[Section 21(1)]

